      <body>
         <div type="edition" xml:lang="tel-Latn">
            <p>
               <lb n="1"/>svasti śrī vaṇavṟōla apimanagaṁgu kessaraju<lb n="2" break="no"/>n iccina datti i ceṟuvuḷa vitara<unclear>ṭṭi</unclear> ve<lb n="3" break="no"/>ṭanivāru baranasiyu ceṟuvu kavila<lb n="4" break="no"/>yun aḻisinavāri <unclear>pā</unclear>paṁ<unclear>bu</unclear> goṇḍṟu veṭaniva<lb n="5" break="no"/>ru bu<unclear>ṭe</unclear>limarammacari sēse
            </p>
         </div>
         <div type="apparatus">
         </div>
         <div type="translation" source="bib:Sastri1969_01">
            <p>
               Hail! Prosperity! Apimanagaṁgu Kessaraju made the grant at Vaṇavrōlu. Those who do not (protect?) these tanks will incur the sin of those who destroy Baranasi, a tank and a cow. Buṭelimarammacari did (i.e. engraved this inscription).
            </p>
         </div>
         <div type="translation" resp="part:jeth">
 	<!--Yet to be provided -->
         </div>
         <div type="commentary">
            <p>
               The text follows the edition of J. Ramayya Pantulu in <bibl rend="omitname"><ptr target="bib:RamayyaPantulu1948_01"/><citedRange unit="page">341</citedRange><citedRange unit="item">633</citedRange></bibl> in absence of a picture. 
            </p>
         </div>
        <div type="bibliography">
	<p>
              The inscription was noted in A. R. No. 811 of 1917 <!-- has to be adjusted to the @target --> and first published by J. Ramayya Pantulu in <bibl rend="omitname"><ptr target="bib:RamayyaPantulu1948_01"/><citedRange unit="page">341</citedRange><citedRange unit="item">633</citedRange></bibl> with few metadata and without translation.
              K. M. Sastry <bibl rend="omitname"><ptr target="bib:Sastri1969_01"/><citedRange unit="page">341</citedRange></bibl> provides a translation while relying on J. Ramayya Pantulu’s edition.
	</p>
